{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>For had we not lingered.</b> Our Rabbi Hananel, of blessed memory, explained: Scripture teaches you that they constrained themselves with [lack of] food and did not cast words against their father until he was persuaded of his own accord, because they treated him with great honor. And once he was persuaded, he counseled them in five matters. <b>The first:</b> 'bring down a present for the man.' <b>The second:</b> 'and take double money in your hand.' <b>The third:</b> 'and the money that was returned' etc. — perhaps it was an oversight: perhaps the overseer of the house forgot it inadvertently; Jacob commanded them to return it on account of the sanctity of the Name. <b>The fourth:</b> 'and take your brother.' <b>The fifth:</b> prayer — he said to them, 'and may El Shaddai grant you compassion before the man.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 43, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:19:59.661449088Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}